<template>
  <div class="row" :class="{ dark: dark }">
    <div class="todo-item" :class="{ completed: completed }">
      <button class="check" @click="on_toggle" :click-payload="index">
        <span class="check-mark" v-if="completed">✓</span>
      </button>
      <div class="todo-text">{{ text }}</div>
      <button class="remove" @click="on_remove" :click-payload="index">×</button>
    </div>
  </div>
</template>

<script setup>
// One row of the list. `Todos` owns the data and the actions; this component
// owns the row's appearance and nothing else.
//
// A note on the two wrappers above, since this parser has no comment syntax of
// its own and every comment in this file lives here or in the style block.
//
// `.row` holds the THEME class and has to be an ancestor rather than the card
// itself: the cascade matches a selector's leftmost part only against a STRICT
// ancestor (velox-style/src/lib.rs `match_prefix` starts one level above the
// target), and it has no way to say an element has two classes —
// `parse_selector_part` reads `.todo-item.dark` as one class literally called
// "todo-item.dark". So an element that HOLDS `.dark` can never be the element a
// `.dark …` rule styles, which is why the theme carrier is unstyled and the
// surface sits one level below it.
//
// `.todo-item` holds the STATE class one level further in, and that second
// level is what makes the combination expressible at all: `.dark .completed
// .check` needs a `.dark` ancestor of a `.completed` ancestor of the box. Both
// carriers are elements this file renders, so every compound in that selector
// gets this component's own scope id and the whole chain matches.
//
// `.todo-text` is a block rather than a bare span because it is the element the
// text sits DIRECTLY in: the text painter wraps at its PARENT's content width
// (velox-renderer/src/skia_render.rs `container_rect`), so a long task has to be
// a direct child of the box that was sized for it, or it wraps at the row's
// width and runs under the remove button.
//
// The check and the remove control are `<button>`s rather than an
// `<input type="checkbox">` because Velox draws that at a fixed 18px with a
// hard-coded tick colour (velox-renderer/src/skia_render.rs:2313), which cannot
// be themed — and because `:hover` only reaches a `<button>`, an element
// carrying `on:click`, or an element whose class is literally `btn`
// (velox-renderer/src/events.rs:150). Both of these need hover.
//
// The ✓ and × above are literal characters, not character references: nothing in
// Velox decodes `&#10003;`. Which of them actually render is a HOST-FONT
// question and only ONE of the two is safe everywhere: × U+00D7 is Latin-1
// Supplement and is in every candidate face, but ✓ U+2713 is NOT in Noto Sans.
// Velox has one face and no glyph fallback, so a missing codepoint paints as
// glyph 0 — a tofu box. `load_default_typeface` therefore prefers DejaVu Sans,
// which has both, and the same face is bundled under
// `velox-renderer/assets/`; the full coverage table is in `App.vx`'s script
// block. Check a new symbol against that table before using it here.
pub struct Props {
    pub todo: String,
    pub completed: bool,
    pub index: String,
    pub dark: bool,
}

pub struct State {
    pub props: Props,
}

impl State {
    pub fn new() -> Self {
        Self {
            props: Props {
                todo: String::new(),
                completed: false,
                index: String::new(),
                dark: false,
            },
        }
    }

    pub fn text(&self) -> String {
        self.props.todo.clone()
    }

    pub fn completed(&self) -> bool {
        self.props.completed
    }

    pub fn index(&self) -> String {
        self.props.index.clone()
    }

    pub fn dark(&self) -> bool {
        self.props.dark
    }

    // Row events bubble to the owning (Todos) State via the root dispatcher;
    // these no-ops keep the generated per-component dispatcher well formed. The
    // `click-payload` carries the row index the parent needs.
    pub fn on_toggle(&self) {}
    pub fn on_remove(&self) {}
}
</script>

<style scoped>
/* The row's own defaults, so the component stands on its own. The two wrappers
   are unstyled: `.row` is a plain block that the list's `gap` spaces, and
   `.todo-item` below is what fills it. */
/* The row's own defaults, so the component stands on its own. The two wrappers
   are unstyled: `.row` is a plain block that the list's `gap` spaces, and
   `.todo-item` below is what fills it. The scales — type, space, surface, ink,
   radius — are declared once, at the top of App.vx. */
.row {
    display: block;
    width: 100%;
    font-family: "Inter", "Noto Sans", "DejaVu Sans", sans-serif;
    font-size: 15px;
    line-height: 1.45;
}
/* A card, so the fill carries the layer and the edge only separates. `#DFDBD2`
   is the decorative token, one step lighter than the `#D8D4CB` it replaces: at
   1.38:1 on the fill it draws a line without drawing a BOX. */
.todo-item {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: row;
    align-items: flex-start;
    gap: 12px;
    width: 100%;
    padding: 12px;
    border: 1px solid #DFDBD2;
    border-radius: 12px;
    background: #ffffff;
}

/* `align-items: flex-start` above is what keeps a two-line task aligned with
   the top of its check instead of drifting to the vertical middle. 20px is the
   smallest step on the control ladder, and at 12px of padding the row's rhythm
   holds whatever the text does. */
.check {
    flex: 0 0 auto;
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
    width: 20px;
    height: 20px;
    padding: 0;
    border: 1px solid #868D92;
    border-radius: 999px;
    background: #ffffff;
    color: #ffffff;
}
.check:hover {
    border: 1px solid #0d6e66;
}
/* U+2713 CHECK MARK, verified present in the bundled face. 12px inside a 20px
   circle is the proportion a check has to have to read as a check. */
.check-mark {
    display: block;
    font-size: 12px;
    font-weight: 700;
    line-height: 1;
    color: #ffffff;
}
/* `padding-top: 1px` is optical, not rhythm: a 15px glyph's cap height sits a
   pixel below the box top, and without it the text reads low against the
   check's circle. */
.todo-text {
    flex: 1 1 auto;
    min-width: 0;
    padding-top: 1px;
    font-size: 15px;
    line-height: 1.45;
    color: #14181b;
}
.remove {
    flex: 0 0 auto;
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
    width: 28px;
    height: 28px;
    padding: 0;
    border: 1px solid transparent;
    border-radius: 8px;
    background: #ffffff;
    color: #5F6A70;
    font-size: 16px;
    line-height: 1;
    /* Its ONLY child is a bare text node — the × — not an element. `justify-
       content` positions flex ITEMS, and a text node is not one, so the × ignores
       the `center` above and sits at the padding edge. `text-align` is what the
       painter actually reads for a text node, and the sibling `.ghost` /
       `.cancel` rules already carry it for the same reason. Without this the ×
       is visibly off-centre in its button. */
    text-align: center;
}
/* The destructive hover is the danger token at full strength, which is the only
   place on the page a row's own chrome turns red. */
.remove:hover {
    border: 1px solid #a3342c;
    background: #a3342c;
    color: #ffffff;
}

/* Completed rows.

   `text-decoration` is INHERITABLE (velox-style/src/lib.rs:761), so the
   declaration on this box reaches the text node inside it, and the painter
   reads it there — `line-through` is drawn as its own band above the baseline
   (velox-renderer/src/skia_render.rs `draw_text_decorations`).

   The state class is on the card and the text is reached as a DESCENDANT of it
   rather than as `.todo-item.completed`: the selector parser takes everything
   after a leading `.` as ONE class name (velox-style/src/lib.rs:382), so
   `.todo-item.completed` looks for a class called "todo-item.completed" and
   matches nothing. */
.completed .check {
    border: 1px solid #0d6e66;
    background: #0d6e66;
}
/* Still a live control when the row is done, so it keeps a hover — just a
   quieter one. */
.completed .check:hover {
    border: 1px solid #0a5750;
    background: #0a5750;
}
/* The muted ink role, so a finished row steps down rather than disappearing. */
.completed .todo-text {
    color: #5F6A70;
    text-decoration: line-through;
}

/* Dark overrides — source order decides the winner (velox-style/src/lib.rs:786
   `apply_styles_with_hover`, cascade loop at :840), so they come last. The `.dark .completed …` pair
   has to come after BOTH `.completed …` and `.dark …` to beat them. */
.dark .todo-item {
    border: 1px solid #313B42;
    background: #141A1E;
}
.dark .check {
    border: 1px solid #64727B;
    background: #141A1E;
    color: #04211D;
}
.dark .check:hover {
    border: 1px solid #2DD4BF;
}
.dark .check-mark {
    color: #04211D;
}
.dark .todo-text {
    color: #EDF2F3;
}
.dark .remove {
    border: 1px solid transparent;
    background: #141A1E;
    color: #849299;
}
.dark .remove:hover {
    border: 1px solid #FF8A80;
    background: #FF8A80;
    color: #2B0704;
}
.dark .completed .check {
    border: 1px solid #2DD4BF;
    background: #2DD4BF;
}
.dark .completed .check:hover {
    border: 1px solid #5EEAD4;
    background: #5EEAD4;
}
.dark .completed .todo-text {
    color: #849299;
}
</style>
